  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\alpha_1, \\alpha_2, \\cdots, \\alpha_n$ are in A.P. with common difference $\\theta$, then the sum of the series $\\sec \\alpha_1 \\sec \\alpha_2+\\sec \\alpha_2 \\sec \\alpha_3+\\cdots \\cdot+\\sec \\alpha_{n-1} \\sec \\alpha_n=k\\left(\\tan \\alpha_n-\\tan \\alpha_1\\right)$ where $k=$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2ZCpa",
      "text": "$\\sin \\theta$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "v2EwL",
      "text": "$\\cos \\theta$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lu98y",
      "text": "$\\sec \\theta$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Rcmul",
      "text": "$\\operatorname{cosec} \\theta$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: $\\alpha_2-\\alpha_1=\\alpha_3-\\alpha_2=\\cdots=\\theta$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{s}=\\frac{1}{\\sin \\theta}\\left[\\frac{\\sin \\left(\\alpha_2-\\alpha_1\\right)}{\\cos \\alpha_2 \\cos \\alpha_1}+\\cdots+\\frac{\\sin \\left(\\alpha_n-\\alpha_{n-1}\\right)}{\\cos \\alpha_n \\cos \\alpha_{n-1}}\\right] \\\\\n& =\\operatorname{cosec} \\theta\\left[\\tan \\alpha_n-\\tan \\alpha_1\\right]\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
